                <pb facs="0832" n="720" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg720"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.512/1963</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Fletcher</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-05-17T12:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 17, 1918, noon.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1078. My 1070, May 14, 2 p.m. Minister for Foreign Affairs informs me that time
                    for filing manifests called for by Article 14 of the petroleum decree of
                    February 14 [19] last has been entered [extended?] until July 31 next and that
                    Cabinet has decided to give the representatives of petroleum interests an
                    opportunity to be heard, and I have so advised Garfield.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Fletcher</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
